- How does Replicaset works?
- Let's suppose we have applied on replicaset file and 5 pods are running all of them would have same configurations except name, if one of them is deleted then that would be automatically created. 
- How do we know that a particular pod is under which resource (Replicaset), so while doing kubectl get pod pod-name -oyaml, if in the yaml there is something present in ownerReferences section then it is under that resource. otherwise it is free to use.
- How to run heterogeneous replicas, for e.g. we want 3 pod, 2 with nginx image and 1 with redis image then we can run a pod with label as release:alpha1.1 with redis image and then run the replicaset yaml with replicaset number = 3 and label as release=alpha1.1 then it will acquire that redis pod and create two new pods with tag as release=alpha1.1, we can verify this by seeing redis pod yaml for ownerReference section.

- How does that downgrade and upgrade happen:
When scaling down, the ReplicaSet controller chooses which pods to delete by sorting the available pods to prioritize scaling down pods based on the following general algorithm:
1. Pending (and unschedulable) pods are scaled down first.
2. If controller.kubernetes.io/pod-deletion-cost annotation is set, then the pod with the lower value will come first.
3. Pods on nodes with more replicas come before pods on nodes with fewer replicas.
4. If the pods' creation times differ, the pod that was created more recently comes before the older pod (the creation times are bucketed on an integer log scale when the LogarithmicScaleDown feature gate is enabled).

